# v2 pipeline artifacts. `/build/*` rather than `/build/`: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a negation under an excluded parent
# never fires and `# Only the tally is tracked. The Stata index is a 1 MB pair of files already
# deposited at 10.5281/zenodo.21926100, so a copy here is duplication that
# also trips the large-file hook.
!/build/release/
/build/release/*
!/build/release/tally/` silently did nothing for months.
/corpus/
/build/*
# Only the tally is tracked. The Stata index is a 1 MB pair of files already
# deposited at 10.5281/zenodo.21926100, so a copy here is duplication that
# also trips the large-file hook.
!/build/release/
/build/release/*
!/build/release/tally/
/registries/snapshots/
/outputs/

# Rendered paper outputs; rebuilt by `make paper`. The PDF is tracked, unlike
# the intermediates: the site serves it and CI cannot rebuild it, because
# rendering the paper needs 57 MB of Parquet that only exists on the machine
# that collected the corpus. Same reason `paper/figures/*.pdf` are tracked.
paper/paper.md
paper/paper.html
paper/figures/*.png

# Generated by `make site`; the tracked inputs are docs/index.md.in and
# build/release/tally/
docs/_build/
docs/_extra/
docs/index.md
docs/data-dictionary.md

# Unsent draft correspondence and working notes. Not publications: they name
# a third party's security posture and carry a personal email address. Kept
# out of the docs source tree so they cannot be rendered by accident.
/notes/
